    {"jp": "雨が止んだから、今夜は屋上で星を見よう。", "en": "The rain has stopped, so let's look at the stars on the roof tonight.", "fr": "La pluie s'est arrêtée, allons regarder les étoiles sur le toit ce soir.", "grammar": "意向形 〜(よ)う", "focus": "屋上"},
    {"jp": "花見の季節だから、日曜日にみんなで出かけよう。", "en": "It's cherry-blossom season, so let's all go out on Sunday.", "fr": "C'est la saison des cerisiers en fleur, sortons tous ensemble dimanche.", "grammar": "意向形 〜(よ)う", "focus": "花見"},
    {"jp": "来年は、外国の文化を研究しようと思っています。", "en": "Next year, I'm thinking of studying foreign cultures.", "fr": "L'année prochaine, je pense faire des recherches sur les cultures étrangères.", "grammar": "〜ようと思う", "focus": "文化"},
    {"jp": "お世話になった先生に、手紙でお礼を伝えようと思います。", "en": "I'm thinking of writing a letter to thank the teacher who did so much for me.", "fr": "Je pense remercier par lettre le professeur qui m'a tant aidé.", "grammar": "〜ようと思う", "focus": "お礼"},
    {"jp": "この階段を下りると、左に港が見えます。", "en": "When you go down these stairs, you can see the harbour on the left.", "fr": "Quand on descend cet escalier, on voit le port sur la gauche.", "grammar": "〜と", "focus": "港"},
    {"jp": "季節が変わって寒くなると、体の具合が悪くなります。", "en": "When the season changes and it turns cold, I start to feel unwell.", "fr": "Quand la saison change et qu'il fait froid, je ne me sens pas bien.", "grammar": "〜と", "focus": "具合"},
    {"jp": "運転しながら、スマホを使ってはいけません。", "en": "You must not use your smartphone while driving.", "fr": "Il ne faut pas utiliser son smartphone en conduisant.", "grammar": "〜ながら", "focus": "スマホ"},
    {"jp": "景色を楽しみながら、森の中をゆっくり歩きました。", "en": "I walked slowly through the forest, enjoying the scenery.", "fr": "J'ai marché lentement dans la forêt en profitant du paysage.", "grammar": "〜ながら", "focus": "景色"},
    {"jp": "休みの日は、漫画を読んだり、テニスをしたりします。", "en": "On my days off, I do things like reading manga and playing tennis.", "fr": "Les jours de repos, je lis des mangas, je joue au tennis, ce genre de choses.", "grammar": "〜たり〜たり", "focus": "漫画"},
    {"jp": "お祭りの夜は、みんなで踊ったり騒いだりしました。", "en": "On the night of the festival, we all danced and had a lively time.", "fr": "Le soir de la fête, nous avons tous dansé et fait la fête ensemble.", "grammar": "〜たり〜たり", "focus": "踊る"},
    {"jp": "旅行中にステーキを食べすぎて、少し太ってしまいました。", "en": "I ate too much steak during the trip and put on a little weight.", "fr": "Pendant le voyage, j'ai mangé trop de steak et j'ai un peu grossi.", "grammar": "〜すぎる", "focus": "太る"},
    {"jp": "先生の説明は細かすぎて、よく分かりませんでした。", "en": "The teacher's explanation was too detailed, and I didn't really understand it.", "fr": "L'explication du professeur était trop détaillée, je n'ai pas bien compris.", "grammar": "〜すぎる", "focus": "説明"},
    {"jp": "この布団は柔らかくて、とても寝やすいです。", "en": "This futon is soft and very easy to sleep on.", "fr": "Ce futon est moelleux, on y dort très bien.", "grammar": "〜やすい／〜にくい", "focus": "布団"},
    {"jp": "この手袋は固くて、指が使いにくいです。", "en": "These gloves are stiff, so it's hard to use my fingers.", "fr": "Ces gants sont rigides, j'ai du mal à me servir de mes doigts.", "grammar": "〜やすい／〜にくい", "focus": "手袋"},
    {"jp": "台風で風が強くなって、木が揺れはじめました。", "en": "The wind picked up with the typhoon and the trees began to sway.", "fr": "Avec le typhon, le vent s'est levé et les arbres ont commencé à se balancer.", "grammar": "〜はじめる／〜おわる／〜つづける", "focus": "揺れる"},
    {"jp": "祖父は亡くなるまで、日記を書きつづけました。", "en": "My grandfather kept writing his diary until he died.", "fr": "Mon grand-père a tenu son journal jusqu'à sa mort.", "grammar": "〜はじめる／〜おわる／〜つづける", "focus": "日記"},
    {"jp": "この町の人口は、これからも増えていくでしょう。", "en": "This town's population will probably keep growing from now on.", "fr": "La population de cette ville va sans doute continuer à augmenter.", "grammar": "〜ていく／〜てくる", "focus": "人口"},
    {"jp": "駅前の店でサンドイッチを買ってくるから、ここで待っていて。", "en": "I'll go and get some sandwiches at the shop in front of the station, so wait here.", "fr": "Je vais acheter des sandwichs au magasin devant la gare, attends-moi ici.", "grammar": "〜ていく／〜てくる", "focus": "サンドイッチ"},
    {"jp": "パンにこのジャムを塗って食べてみてください。", "en": "Spread this jam on some bread and try it.", "fr": "Tartinez un peu de cette confiture sur du pain et goûtez, pour voir.", "grammar": "〜てみる", "focus": "塗る"},
    {"jp": "分からないときは、先輩に相談してみたらどうですか。", "en": "When you don't understand something, why not try asking a senior colleague for advice?", "fr": "Quand vous ne comprenez pas, pourquoi ne pas essayer de demander conseil à un aîné ?", "grammar": "〜てみる", "focus": "相談"},
    {"jp": "会社の受付に、季節の花が飾ってあります。", "en": "Seasonal flowers have been arranged at the company's reception desk.", "fr": "À l'accueil de l'entreprise, on a disposé des fleurs de saison.", "grammar": "〜てある", "focus": "飾る"},
    {"jp": "引き出しの中に、住所を書いた紙が入れてあります。", "en": "A piece of paper with the address on it has been put in the drawer.", "fr": "On a mis dans le tiroir un papier où est écrite l'adresse.", "grammar": "〜てある", "focus": "住所"},
    {"jp": "郊外に新しい美術館ができるらしいです。", "en": "Apparently a new art museum is going to open in the suburbs.", "fr": "Il paraît qu'un nouveau musée d'art va ouvrir en banlieue.", "grammar": "〜らしい", "focus": "美術館"},
    {"jp": "部長の息子さんは、大学の入学試験に落ちたらしいです。", "en": "Apparently the department head's son failed his university entrance exam.", "fr": "Il paraît que le fils du chef de service a échoué à son examen d'entrée à l'université.", "grammar": "〜らしい", "focus": "落ちる"},
    {"jp": "あの店員、今日はずいぶんいそがしいみたいだね。", "en": "That shop assistant seems really busy today.", "fr": "Ce vendeur a l'air vraiment débordé aujourd'hui.", "grammar": "〜みたいだ", "focus": "店員"},
    {"jp": "この人形は、まるで生きているみたいだね。", "en": "This doll looks just like it's alive.", "fr": "Cette poupée, on dirait vraiment qu'elle est vivante.", "grammar": "〜みたいだ", "focus": "人形"},
    {"jp": "母が入院したので、私が家族の食事を作ることになりました。", "en": "My mother has gone into hospital, so it's fallen to me to cook the family's meals.", "fr": "Ma mère a été hospitalisée, c'est donc moi qui vais préparer les repas de la famille.", "grammar": "〜ことになる", "focus": "入院"},
    {"jp": "父の仕事の都合で、アメリカに引っ越すことになりました。", "en": "Because of my father's work, it's been decided that we'll move to America.", "fr": "Pour le travail de mon père, nous allons devoir déménager aux États-Unis.", "grammar": "〜ことになる", "focus": "都合"},
    {"jp": "寝る前に、必ず次の日の支度をするようにしています。", "en": "I make a point of always getting ready for the next day before going to bed.", "fr": "Je prends soin de toujours préparer mes affaires du lendemain avant de me coucher.", "grammar": "〜ようにする", "focus": "支度"},
    {"jp": "講義では、なるべく自分の意見を言うようにしています。", "en": "In lectures, I try to give my own opinion as much as possible.", "fr": "En cours, je m'efforce de donner mon avis autant que possible.", "grammar": "〜ようにする", "focus": "なるべく"},
    {"jp": "会議に間に合うかどうか、少し心配です。", "en": "I'm a little worried about whether I'll make it to the meeting in time.", "fr": "Je m'inquiète un peu de savoir si j'arriverai à temps à la réunion.", "grammar": "〜かどうか", "focus": "間に合う"},
    {"jp": "今度の試合に出られるかどうか、まだ決まっていません。", "en": "It hasn't been decided yet whether I can play in the next match.", "fr": "On n'a pas encore décidé si je pourrai jouer le prochain match.", "grammar": "〜かどうか", "focus": "試合"},
    {"jp": "駐車場には車が三台しかとめられません。", "en": "Only three cars can be parked in the car park.", "fr": "On ne peut garer que trois voitures sur le parking.", "grammar": "〜しか〜ない", "focus": "駐車場"},
    {"jp": "旅行の最後の日には、財布に千円しか残っていなかった。", "en": "On the last day of the trip, I had only a thousand yen left in my wallet.", "fr": "Le dernier jour du voyage, il ne me restait que mille yens dans mon portefeuille.", "grammar": "〜しか〜ない", "focus": "残る"},
    {"jp": "何度注意しても、息子は部屋を片付けません。", "en": "No matter how many times I tell him, my son won't tidy his room.", "fr": "J'ai beau le lui répéter, mon fils ne range pas sa chambre.", "grammar": "〜ても", "focus": "注意"},
    {"jp": "少し熱があっても、大事な会議には出席します。", "en": "Even if I have a slight fever, I will attend the important meeting.", "fr": "Même si j'ai un peu de fièvre, j'assisterai à la réunion importante.", "grammar": "〜ても", "focus": "出席"},
    {"jp": "部長、会議室でお客さんがお待ちになっています。", "en": "Sir, a client is waiting for you in the meeting room.", "fr": "Monsieur, un client vous attend dans la salle de réunion.", "grammar": "お〜になる／お〜する", "focus": "会議室"},
    {"jp": "先輩、その重い道具は私がお持ちします。", "en": "Let me carry those heavy tools for you.", "fr": "Laissez-moi porter ces outils lourds pour vous.", "grammar": "お〜になる／お〜する", "focus": "道具"},
    {"jp": "すみません、けさ寝坊して電車に間に合わなかったんです。", "en": "I'm sorry — I overslept this morning and missed the train, you see.", "fr": "Désolé, c'est que je me suis réveillé en retard ce matin et que j'ai raté le train.", "grammar": "〜んです／〜のです", "focus": "寝坊"},
    {"jp": "あの店員さんは、どうしてそんなに怒っているんですか。", "en": "Why is that shop assistant so angry?", "fr": "Pourquoi ce vendeur est-il donc si en colère ?", "grammar": "〜んです／〜のです", "focus": "怒る"},
    {"jp": "息子にはもう少し丁寧に字を書いてほしいです。", "en": "I'd like my son to write his characters a little more carefully.", "fr": "J'aimerais que mon fils écrive ses caractères un peu plus soigneusement.", "grammar": "〜てほしい", "focus": "字"},
    {"jp": "夫には、休みの日くらい子どもの世話をしてほしい。", "en": "I want my husband to look after the children, at least on his days off.", "fr": "J'aimerais que mon mari s'occupe des enfants, au moins ses jours de congé.", "grammar": "〜てほしい", "focus": "世話"},
    {"jp": "娘は毎晩、寝る前に漫画を読みたがります。", "en": "Every night before bed, my daughter wants to read manga.", "fr": "Tous les soirs avant de dormir, ma fille veut lire des mangas.", "grammar": "〜たがる", "focus": "漫画"},
    {"jp": "祖母は具合が悪いのに、入院したがらない。", "en": "My grandmother is unwell, yet she doesn't want to go into hospital.", "fr": "Ma grand-mère est souffrante, mais elle ne veut pas être hospitalisée.", "grammar": "〜たがる", "focus": "入院"},
    {"jp": "みんなの意見が合わないので、計画はまだ決まりそうにない。", "en": "Since everyone's opinions differ, it doesn't look as if the plan will be settled yet.", "fr": "Comme les avis ne s'accordent pas, le projet n'est pas près d'être arrêté.", "grammar": "〜そうにない", "focus": "意見"},
    {"jp": "台風が近いので、飛行機は出発できそうにありません。", "en": "With the typhoon close by, the plane doesn't look likely to take off.", "fr": "Avec le typhon tout proche, l'avion ne semble pas près de pouvoir décoller.", "grammar": "〜そうにない", "focus": "台風"},
    {"jp": "あしたは朝早く、空港まで妻を迎えに行かなくてはいけない。", "en": "Tomorrow I have to go to the airport early in the morning to pick up my wife.", "fr": "Demain, je dois aller chercher ma femme à l'aéroport tôt le matin.", "grammar": "〜なくてはいけない", "focus": "迎える"},
    {"jp": "このレポートは金曜日までに、課長に送らなくてはいけません。", "en": "I have to send this report to the section manager by Friday.", "fr": "Je dois envoyer ce rapport au chef de section d'ici vendredi.", "grammar": "〜なくてはいけない", "focus": "課長"},
    {"jp": "もうこんな時間か。急がなきゃ、特急が出ちゃう。", "en": "Is it this late already? I've got to hurry or the express will leave without me.", "fr": "Déjà cette heure-là ? Il faut que je me dépêche, sinon l'express va partir sans moi.", "grammar": "〜なきゃ／〜なくちゃ", "focus": "特急"},
    {"jp": "あしたは試験だから、今夜は復習しなくちゃ。", "en": "I've got an exam tomorrow, so I have to review tonight.", "fr": "J'ai un examen demain, alors ce soir il faut que je révise.", "grammar": "〜なきゃ／〜なくちゃ", "focus": "復習"},
    {"jp": "引っ越す前に、新しい住所を会社に知らせないといけない。", "en": "Before I move, I need to let the company know my new address.", "fr": "Avant de déménager, je dois communiquer ma nouvelle adresse à l'entreprise.", "grammar": "〜ないといけない", "focus": "住所"},
    {"jp": "このけがには、毎日、朝と晩に薬を塗らないといけません。", "en": "You have to put medicine on this injury every morning and evening.", "fr": "Il faut appliquer le médicament sur cette blessure tous les jours, matin et soir.", "grammar": "〜ないといけない", "focus": "塗る"},
    {"jp": "この旅館は景色もいいし、料理もおいしいし、また泊まりたい。", "en": "This inn has a lovely view and good food, so I'd like to stay here again.", "fr": "Dans cette auberge, la vue est belle et la cuisine est bonne : j'aimerais y loger à nouveau.", "grammar": "〜し", "focus": "景色"},
    {"jp": "今日は熱もあるし、のども痛いし、会社を休もう。", "en": "I've got a fever, and my throat hurts too, so I'll take the day off work.", "fr": "J'ai de la fièvre, et mal à la gorge en plus : aujourd'hui, je ne vais pas au travail.", "grammar": "〜し", "focus": "のど"},
    {"jp": "西の空に黒い雲が増えてきた。夜には雨が降るだろう。", "en": "Dark clouds are gathering in the western sky. It will probably rain tonight.", "fr": "Des nuages noirs s'amoncellent à l'ouest. Il pleuvra sans doute ce soir.", "grammar": "〜だろう", "focus": "雲"},
    {"jp": "彼はまじめだから、きっと約束の時間に来るだろう。", "en": "He's conscientious, so he'll surely come at the agreed time.", "fr": "Il est sérieux, alors il viendra sûrement à l'heure convenue.", "grammar": "〜だろう", "focus": "約束"},
    {"jp": "誕生日にこのケーキをあげたら、母は喜ぶかな。", "en": "I wonder if my mother will be pleased if I give her this cake for her birthday.", "fr": "Je me demande si ce gâteau fera plaisir à ma mère pour son anniversaire.", "grammar": "〜かな", "focus": "喜ぶ"},
    {"jp": "今度の花見、雨が降らないといいけど、大丈夫かな。", "en": "I hope it doesn't rain for our next cherry-blossom viewing — I wonder if it'll be all right.", "fr": "Pourvu qu'il ne pleuve pas pour notre prochaine sortie sous les cerisiers… je me demande si ça ira.", "grammar": "〜かな", "focus": "花見"},
    {"jp": "昔の写真でいちばん驚いたのは、父の長い髪だ。", "en": "What surprised me most in the old photos was my father's long hair.", "fr": "Ce qui m'a le plus surpris sur les vieilles photos, ce sont les cheveux longs de mon père.", "grammar": "〜のは〜だ", "focus": "髪"},
    {"jp": "この仕事で大事なのは、お客さんへの丁寧なあいさつだ。", "en": "What matters in this job is greeting customers politely.", "fr": "Dans ce travail, ce qui compte, c'est de saluer poliment les clients.", "grammar": "〜のは〜だ", "focus": "あいさつ"},
    {"jp": "僕の趣味は、近所の川で魚を釣ることです。", "en": "My hobby is fishing in the river near my home.", "fr": "Mon passe-temps, c'est de pêcher dans la rivière près de chez moi.", "grammar": "〜こと", "focus": "趣味"},
    {"jp": "毎日少しずつ運動を続けることが大切です。", "en": "It's important to keep up a little exercise every day.", "fr": "Il est important de continuer à faire un peu d'exercice chaque jour.", "grammar": "〜こと", "focus": "運動"},
    {"jp": "小さな子どもが一人で坂を下りていくのを見て、心配になった。", "en": "Seeing a small child going down the slope alone, I got worried.", "fr": "En voyant un petit enfant descendre la pente tout seul, je me suis inquiété.", "grammar": "〜の", "focus": "坂"},
    {"jp": "夜、湖の周りを散歩するのは気持ちがいい。", "en": "Taking a walk around the lake at night feels good.", "fr": "Se promener autour du lac le soir, c'est agréable.", "grammar": "〜の", "focus": "湖"},
    {"jp": "家を出る前に、天気予報を調べればよかった。", "en": "I should have checked the weather forecast before leaving the house.", "fr": "J'aurais dû regarder la météo avant de quitter la maison.", "grammar": "〜ばよかった", "focus": "天気予報"},
    {"jp": "親切な店員さんに、あんなひどいことを言わなければよかった。", "en": "I wish I hadn't said such awful things to that kind shop assistant.", "fr": "Je n'aurais pas dû dire des choses aussi méchantes à cette vendeuse si gentille.", "grammar": "〜ばよかった", "focus": "店員"},
    {"jp": "そんなに眠いなら、昼休みに少し寝たらどうですか。", "en": "If you're that sleepy, why not sleep a little during your lunch break?", "fr": "Si vous avez tellement sommeil, pourquoi ne pas dormir un peu pendant la pause de midi ?", "grammar": "〜たらどうですか", "focus": "眠い"},
    {"jp": "道が分からないなら、駅前の交番で尋ねたらどうですか。", "en": "If you don't know the way, why not ask at the police box in front of the station?", "fr": "Si vous ne connaissez pas le chemin, pourquoi ne pas demander au poste de police devant la gare ?", "grammar": "〜たらどうですか", "focus": "尋ねる"},
    {"jp": "彼は誰にも相談せずに、会社をやめてしまった。", "en": "He quit the company without consulting anyone.", "fr": "Il a quitté l'entreprise sans en parler à personne.", "grammar": "〜ずに", "focus": "相談"},
    {"jp": "辞書を使わずに、この小説を最後まで読んだ。", "en": "I read this novel to the end without using a dictionary.", "fr": "J'ai lu ce roman jusqu'au bout sans utiliser de dictionnaire.", "grammar": "〜ずに", "focus": "小説"},
    {"jp": "家族旅行で留守にしているあいだに、泥棒に入られた。", "en": "While we were away on a family trip, our house was burgled.", "fr": "Pendant que nous étions partis en voyage en famille, nous avons été cambriolés.", "grammar": "〜あいだに", "focus": "泥棒"},
    {"jp": "あかちゃんが眠っているあいだに、急いで洗濯をした。", "en": "While the baby was asleep, I hurriedly did the laundry.", "fr": "Pendant que le bébé dormait, j'ai vite fait la lessive.", "grammar": "〜あいだに", "focus": "眠る"},
    {"jp": "講義のあいだ、隣の席の学生はずっと眠っていた。", "en": "Throughout the lecture, the student in the next seat was asleep.", "fr": "Pendant tout le cours, l'étudiant assis à côté de moi a dormi.", "grammar": "〜あいだ", "focus": "講義"},
    {"jp": "夏休みのあいだ、祖母の田舎で毎日泳いでいた。", "en": "All through the summer holidays, I swam every day in the countryside at my grandmother's.", "fr": "Pendant toutes les vacances d'été, je nageais tous les jours à la campagne, chez ma grand-mère.", "grammar": "〜あいだ", "focus": "田舎"},
    {"jp": "ちょうど今から、近所の神社のお祭りに行くところです。", "en": "I'm just about to go to the festival at the local shrine.", "fr": "Je suis justement sur le point d'aller à la fête du sanctuaire du quartier.", "grammar": "〜ところだ", "focus": "神社"},
    {"jp": "彼女は今、空港に向かっているところです。", "en": "She is on her way to the airport right now.", "fr": "Elle est justement en route pour l'aéroport en ce moment.", "grammar": "〜ところだ", "focus": "空港"},
    {"jp": "このパソコンは買ったばかりなのに、もう故障した。", "en": "I only just bought this computer, but it has already broken down.", "fr": "Je viens d'acheter cet ordinateur, et il est déjà en panne.", "grammar": "〜たばかり", "focus": "故障"},
    {"jp": "日本に来たばかりのころは、珍しい習慣によく驚いた。", "en": "When I had just come to Japan, I was often surprised by unusual customs.", "fr": "Quand je venais d'arriver au Japon, des coutumes inhabituelles me surprenaient souvent.", "grammar": "〜たばかり", "focus": "習慣"},
    {"jp": "事故の原因は、私から説明させてください。", "en": "Please let me explain the cause of the accident myself.", "fr": "Permettez-moi d'expliquer moi-même la cause de l'accident.", "grammar": "〜させてください", "focus": "原因"},
    {"jp": "その話は、一度家内と相談させてください。", "en": "Please let me talk that over with my wife first.", "fr": "Pour cette question, laissez-moi d'abord en parler avec ma femme.", "grammar": "〜させてください", "focus": "家内"},
    {"jp": "晩ご飯の前に、出したおもちゃを全部片付けなさい。", "en": "Before dinner, put away all the toys you got out.", "fr": "Avant le dîner, range tous les jouets que tu as sortis.", "grammar": "〜なさい", "focus": "片付ける"},
    {"jp": "この角は車がよく見えないから、渡るときは注意しなさい。", "en": "You can't see the cars well at this corner, so be careful when you cross.", "fr": "À ce coin, on voit mal les voitures, alors fais attention en traversant.", "grammar": "〜なさい", "focus": "注意"},
    {"jp": "ねえ、会社の帰りに駅前で卵を買ってきて。", "en": "Hey, pick up some eggs by the station on your way home from work.", "fr": "Dis, en rentrant du travail, achète-moi des œufs près de la gare.", "grammar": "〜て／〜ないで（依頼）", "focus": "帰り"},
    {"jp": "この壁はまだ乾いていないから、触らないで。", "en": "This wall isn't dry yet, so don't touch it.", "fr": "Ce mur n'est pas encore sec, alors n'y touche pas.", "grammar": "〜て／〜ないで（依頼）", "focus": "壁"},
    {"jp": "将来、医者になるために、毎晩数学を勉強している。", "en": "I study maths every night so that I can become a doctor one day.", "fr": "Pour devenir médecin plus tard, j'étudie les maths tous les soirs.", "grammar": "〜ために", "focus": "将来"},
    {"jp": "事故のために、急行が三十分も遅れました。", "en": "Because of an accident, the express was thirty minutes late.", "fr": "À cause d'un accident, l'express a eu trente minutes de retard.", "grammar": "〜ために", "focus": "事故"},
    {"jp": "試験に遅れないように、いつもより一本早い電車に乗った。", "en": "So as not to be late for the exam, I took the train before my usual one.", "fr": "Pour ne pas être en retard à l'examen, j'ai pris le train d'avant celui que je prends d'habitude.", "grammar": "〜ように", "focus": "試験"},
    {"jp": "ぬれた坂で滑らないように、ゆっくり歩いてください。", "en": "Walk slowly so that you don't slip on the wet slope.", "fr": "Marchez lentement pour ne pas glisser sur la pente mouillée.", "grammar": "〜ように", "focus": "滑る"},
    {"jp": "母に、着物の正しい着方を教えてもらいました。", "en": "My mother taught me the proper way to wear a kimono.", "fr": "Ma mère m'a appris la bonne façon de porter un kimono.", "grammar": "〜方", "focus": "着物"},
    {"jp": "先輩が、会議室の予約の取り方を教えてくれた。", "en": "A senior colleague showed me how to book the meeting room.", "fr": "Un collègue plus ancien m'a montré comment réserver la salle de réunion.", "grammar": "〜方", "focus": "先輩"},
    {"jp": "弟は試合に負けると、いつもすぐに泣き出す。", "en": "Whenever my little brother loses a match, he bursts into tears straight away.", "fr": "Chaque fois que mon petit frère perd un match, il fond aussitôt en larmes.", "grammar": "〜出す", "focus": "負ける"},
    {"jp": "冬が終わって暖かくなると、虫が動き出す。", "en": "When winter ends and it gets warmer, the insects start to stir.", "fr": "Quand l'hiver se termine et qu'il fait plus doux, les insectes se mettent à bouger.", "grammar": "〜出す", "focus": "虫"},
    {"jp": "作文の字が汚かったので、最初から全部書き直すことにした。", "en": "My handwriting in the composition was messy, so I decided to rewrite the whole thing from the start.", "fr": "L'écriture de ma rédaction était peu soignée, alors j'ai décidé de tout réécrire depuis le début.", "grammar": "〜直す", "focus": "最初"},
    {"jp": "部長は、この計画を一から考え直すと言っていた。", "en": "The department head said he would rethink this plan from scratch.", "fr": "Le chef de service a dit qu'il allait repenser ce projet de zéro.", "grammar": "〜直す", "focus": "計画"},
    {"jp": "すみません、この荷物を旅館まで届けてもらえませんか。", "en": "Excuse me, could you deliver this luggage to the inn?", "fr": "Excusez-moi, pourriez-vous livrer ces bagages à l'auberge ?", "grammar": "〜てもらえませんか", "focus": "届ける"},
    {"jp": "この文法の意味を、もう一度説明してもらえませんか。", "en": "Could you explain what this grammar means once more?", "fr": "Pourriez-vous m'expliquer encore une fois le sens de cette grammaire ?", "grammar": "〜てもらえませんか", "focus": "文法"},
    {"jp": "台所から、魚を焼くいいにおいがする。", "en": "There's a lovely smell of fish grilling coming from the kitchen.", "fr": "Une bonne odeur de poisson grillé vient de la cuisine.", "grammar": "〜がする", "focus": "焼く"},
    {"jp": "隣の部屋から、きれいなピアノの音がする。", "en": "The lovely sound of a piano is coming from the next room.", "fr": "On entend un joli son de piano venant de la pièce d'à côté.", "grammar": "〜がする", "focus": "ピアノ"},
    {"jp": "お祝いのパーティーが始まるまでに、会場をきれいに飾っておこう。", "en": "Let's decorate the venue nicely before the celebration party starts.", "fr": "Décorons joliment la salle avant le début de la fête.", "grammar": "〜までに", "focus": "飾る"},
    {"jp": "社長に頼まれた翻訳を、あしたの朝までに終わらせたい。", "en": "I want to finish the translation the company president asked me for by tomorrow morning.", "fr": "Je veux terminer d'ici demain matin la traduction que le président m'a demandée.", "grammar": "〜までに", "focus": "翻訳"},
    {"jp": "けさの地震で、駅前のビルの窓ガラスが割れたそうです。", "en": "I hear this morning's earthquake broke the windows of a building in front of the station.", "fr": "Il paraît que le séisme de ce matin a brisé les vitres d'un immeuble devant la gare.", "grammar": "〜そうだ（伝聞）", "focus": "地震"},
    {"jp": "課長の話では、来月から会社の規則が変わるそうです。", "en": "According to the section manager, the company rules are changing from next month.", "fr": "D'après le chef de section, le règlement de l'entreprise change à partir du mois prochain.", "grammar": "〜そうだ（伝聞）", "focus": "規則"},
    {"jp": "予約を変える場合は、必ず前の日までに連絡してください。", "en": "If you change your reservation, be sure to contact us by the day before.", "fr": "Si vous modifiez votre réservation, prévenez-nous impérativement la veille au plus tard.", "grammar": "〜場合", "focus": "予約"},
    {"jp": "けがをした場合は、受付の人を呼んでください。", "en": "If you get injured, call the reception staff.", "fr": "En cas de blessure, appelez le personnel de l'accueil.", "grammar": "〜場合", "focus": "けが"},
    {"jp": "引っ越す前に、新しい住所を会社に知らせる必要がある。", "en": "Before moving, I need to let my company know my new address.", "fr": "Avant de déménager, je dois communiquer ma nouvelle adresse à mon entreprise.", "grammar": "〜必要がある", "focus": "住所"},
    {"jp": "熱が下がらなかったら、もう一度、病院に行く必要があります。", "en": "If your fever doesn't go down, you'll need to go to the hospital again.", "fr": "Si votre fièvre ne baisse pas, il faudra retourner à l'hôpital.", "grammar": "〜必要がある", "focus": "熱"},
    {"jp": "だから、もっと早く空港へ出発しろと言ったじゃないか。", "en": "See? I told you to leave for the airport earlier, didn't I!", "fr": "Tu vois ? Je t'avais bien dit de partir plus tôt pour l'aéroport !", "grammar": "〜じゃないか", "focus": "出発"},
    {"jp": "君が作ったこのケーキ、すごくうまいじゃないか。", "en": "Hey, this cake you made is really good!", "fr": "Mais il est vraiment bon, ce gâteau que tu as fait !", "grammar": "〜じゃないか", "focus": "ケーキ"},
    {"jp": "息子は注射を怖がるから、病院には行きたくないと言う。", "en": "My son is scared of injections, so he says he doesn't want to go to the hospital.", "fr": "Mon fils a peur des piqûres, alors il dit qu'il ne veut pas aller à l'hôpital.", "grammar": "〜がる", "focus": "注射"},
    {"jp": "夫が留守の日は、娘がいつも寂しがる。", "en": "On days my husband is away, my daughter always seems lonely.", "fr": "Les jours où mon mari est absent, ma fille a toujours l'air de se sentir seule.", "grammar": "〜がる", "focus": "留守"},
    {"jp": "部屋が冷えてきたから、暖房を少し強くするね。", "en": "The room's getting cold, so I'll turn the heating up a little.", "fr": "La pièce se refroidit, je vais monter un peu le chauffage.", "grammar": "〜くする／〜にする", "focus": "暖房"},
    {"jp": "お客さんが泊まるので、押し入れの中をきれいにする。", "en": "We have guests staying the night, so I'm going to clean out the closet.", "fr": "Comme des invités viennent dormir, je vais ranger le placard.", "grammar": "〜くする／〜にする", "focus": "押し入れ"},
    {"jp": "この島には、絵のような美しい景色がある。", "en": "This island has scenery as beautiful as a painting.", "fr": "Cette île offre des paysages beaux comme un tableau.", "grammar": "〜ような", "focus": "景色"},
    {"jp": "彼のような親切な人に会ったのは初めてだ。", "en": "It's the first time I've met someone as kind as him.", "fr": "C'est la première fois que je rencontre quelqu'un d'aussi gentil que lui.", "grammar": "〜ような", "focus": "親切"},
    {"jp": "食料品の売り場は、エスカレーターを下りた所でございます。", "en": "The grocery department is just at the bottom of the escalator.", "fr": "Le rayon alimentation se trouve en bas de l'escalator.", "grammar": "〜でございます", "focus": "食料品"},
    {"jp": "こちらの着物は、どれも絹でございます。", "en": "These kimonos are all silk.", "fr": "Ces kimonos sont tous en soie.", "grammar": "〜でございます", "focus": "絹"},
    {"jp": "社長が会場にいらっしゃったら、私に知らせてください。", "en": "When the company president arrives at the venue, please let me know.", "fr": "Quand le PDG arrivera dans la salle, prévenez-moi, s'il vous plaît.", "grammar": "いらっしゃる／おっしゃる／なさる", "focus": "会場"},
    {"jp": "ご主人は、趣味で何をなさっていますか。", "en": "What does your husband do as a hobby?", "fr": "Que fait votre mari comme loisir ?", "grammar": "いらっしゃる／おっしゃる／なさる", "focus": "趣味"},
    {"jp": "会場の準備は、私たちがいたしますので、ご安心ください。", "en": "We will take care of preparing the venue, so please don't worry.", "fr": "Nous nous chargeons de préparer la salle, soyez donc rassuré.", "grammar": "まいる／もうす／いたす", "focus": "会場"},
    {"jp": "あしたの朝、駅前までお迎えにまいります。", "en": "I will come to pick you up in front of the station tomorrow morning.", "fr": "Demain matin, je viendrai vous chercher devant la gare.", "grammar": "まいる／もうす／いたす", "focus": "駅前"},
    {"jp": "先輩が文法を丁寧に説明してくださった。", "en": "My senior kindly explained the grammar to me carefully.", "fr": "Mon aîné a eu la gentillesse de m'expliquer la grammaire en détail.", "grammar": "〜てくださる／〜ていただく", "focus": "文法"},
    {"jp": "運転手さんに、重い荷物を運んでいただきました。", "en": "The driver kindly carried my heavy luggage for me.", "fr": "Le chauffeur a eu la gentillesse de porter mes lourds bagages.", "grammar": "〜てくださる／〜ていただく", "focus": "運転手"},
    {"jp": "どうぞ、空いている席におかけください。", "en": "Please take any free seat.", "fr": "Je vous en prie, asseyez-vous à une place libre.", "grammar": "お〜ください", "focus": "席"},
    {"jp": "雨で道が滑りますので、足元に注意してお進みください。", "en": "The road is slippery from the rain, so please watch your step as you go.", "fr": "La route est glissante à cause de la pluie : avancez en faisant attention où vous mettez les pieds.", "grammar": "お〜ください", "focus": "足元"},
    {"jp": "歯医者は、寝る前に必ず歯をみがくように言った。", "en": "The dentist told me to always brush my teeth before bed.", "fr": "Le dentiste m'a dit de toujours me brosser les dents avant de dormir.", "grammar": "〜ように言う", "focus": "歯医者"},
    {"jp": "部長は私に、会議の時間を皆に伝えるように言った。", "en": "The department head told me to let everyone know the meeting time.", "fr": "Le chef de département m'a dit de communiquer l'heure de la réunion à tout le monde.", "grammar": "〜ように言う", "focus": "伝える"},
    {"jp": "この説明を英語に翻訳していただけませんか。", "en": "Could you possibly translate this explanation into English?", "fr": "Pourriez-vous traduire cette explication en anglais ?", "grammar": "〜ていただけませんか", "focus": "翻訳"},
    {"jp": "すみません、駐車場の場所を教えていただけませんか。", "en": "Excuse me, could you tell me where the car park is?", "fr": "Excusez-moi, pourriez-vous m'indiquer où se trouve le parking ?", "grammar": "〜ていただけませんか", "focus": "駐車場"},
    {"jp": "地震が来る前に、水を用意しておいてよかった。", "en": "I'm glad I had water ready before the earthquake came.", "fr": "Heureusement que j'avais préparé de l'eau avant le tremblement de terre.", "grammar": "〜てよかった", "focus": "地震"},
    {"jp": "先輩に、将来のことを相談してよかった。", "en": "I'm glad I talked to my senior about my future.", "fr": "Je suis content d'avoir parlé de mon avenir avec mon aîné.", "grammar": "〜てよかった", "focus": "将来"},
    {"jp": "工場の中は危険だから、この線から先へ入るな。", "en": "It's dangerous inside the factory, so don't go past this line.", "fr": "C'est dangereux dans l'usine, alors ne dépasse pas cette ligne.", "grammar": "〜な（禁止）", "focus": "危険"},
    {"jp": "電車の中で騒ぐなと、先生に厳しく注意された。", "en": "The teacher sternly told us not to make a racket on the train.", "fr": "Le professeur nous a sévèrement dit de ne pas chahuter dans le train.", "grammar": "〜な（禁止）", "focus": "騒ぐ"},
    {"jp": "試合はまだ終わっていない。最後まで頑張れ。", "en": "The match isn't over yet. Keep fighting to the end!", "fr": "Le match n'est pas fini. Tiens bon jusqu'au bout !", "grammar": "命令形 〜ろ／〜え", "focus": "試合"},
    {"jp": "火事だ。危ないから、早くこっちへ逃げろ。", "en": "Fire! It's dangerous, so get over here, quick!", "fr": "Au feu ! C'est dangereux, viens vite par ici !", "grammar": "命令形 〜ろ／〜え", "focus": "火事"},
    {"jp": "土曜日の花見までに、雨が止むといいですね。", "en": "I hope the rain stops before the cherry-blossom viewing on Saturday.", "fr": "Pourvu que la pluie cesse avant d'aller voir les cerisiers en fleurs samedi.", "grammar": "〜といい／〜たらいい／〜ばいい", "focus": "花見"},
    {"jp": "駅への道が分からなければ、店員に尋ねればいい。", "en": "If you don't know the way to the station, just ask a shop assistant.", "fr": "Si tu ne connais pas le chemin de la gare, tu n'as qu'à demander à un vendeur.", "grammar": "〜といい／〜たらいい／〜ばいい", "focus": "尋ねる"},
    {"jp": "具合が悪いなら、今夜は無理をしないほうがいいよ。", "en": "If you're feeling unwell, you'd better not overdo it tonight.", "fr": "Si tu ne te sens pas bien, tu ferais mieux de ne pas forcer ce soir.", "grammar": "〜ないほうがいい", "focus": "具合"},
    {"jp": "大事な話は、メールで伝えないほうがいいと思う。", "en": "I think you'd better not pass on important matters by email.", "fr": "Je pense qu'il vaut mieux ne pas annoncer les choses importantes par e-mail.", "grammar": "〜ないほうがいい", "focus": "大事"},
    {"jp": "この湖は、深さが百メートルもあるそうだ。", "en": "Apparently this lake is a full hundred metres deep.", "fr": "Il paraît que ce lac fait pas moins de cent mètres de profondeur.", "grammar": "〜さ", "focus": "湖"},
    {"jp": "何度飲んでも、この薬の苦さには慣れない。", "en": "No matter how many times I take it, I can't get used to how bitter this medicine is.", "fr": "J'ai beau le prendre et le reprendre, je ne m'habitue pas à l'amertume de ce médicament.", "grammar": "〜さ", "focus": "苦い"},
    {"jp": "息子は今、運転中なので、あとで返事をさせます。", "en": "My son is driving right now, so I'll have him get back to you later.", "fr": "Mon fils est en train de conduire, je lui dirai de vous répondre plus tard.", "grammar": "〜中", "focus": "返事"},
    {"jp": "食事中に電話が鳴って、びっくりした。", "en": "The phone rang in the middle of the meal and made me jump.", "fr": "Le téléphone a sonné pendant le repas et ça m'a fait sursauter.", "grammar": "〜中", "focus": "鳴る"},
    {"jp": "退院してからも、一週間おきに病院に通っている。", "en": "Even since being discharged, I've been going back to the hospital every other week.", "fr": "Même depuis ma sortie de l'hôpital, j'y retourne une semaine sur deux.", "grammar": "〜おきに", "focus": "通う"},
    {"jp": "この港から島へは、二時間おきにふねが出ている。", "en": "Boats leave this harbour for the island every two hours.", "fr": "Des bateaux partent de ce port pour l'île toutes les deux heures.", "grammar": "〜おきに", "focus": "港"},
    {"jp": "かぎが見つからなくて、約束の時間に遅れてしまった。", "en": "I couldn't find my keys, so I was late for my appointment.", "fr": "Je ne trouvais pas mes clés, alors je suis arrivé en retard à mon rendez-vous.", "grammar": "〜なくて", "focus": "約束"},
    {"jp": "私が探しているのは辞典じゃなくて、小説です。", "en": "What I'm looking for is not a dictionary but a novel.", "fr": "Ce que je cherche, ce n'est pas un dictionnaire mais un roman.", "grammar": "〜なくて", "focus": "小説"},
    {"jp": "娘が、行きたい高校に入学できますように。", "en": "May my daughter get into the high school she wants.", "fr": "Pourvu que ma fille entre au lycée qu'elle souhaite.", "grammar": "〜ますように", "focus": "入学"},
    {"jp": "祖母のけがが早く治りますように、と神社で祈った。", "en": "I prayed at the shrine that my grandmother's injury would heal quickly.", "fr": "J'ai prié au sanctuaire pour que la blessure de ma grand-mère guérisse vite.", "grammar": "〜ますように", "focus": "神社"},
    {"jp": "会議の場所がどこに決まったか、知っていますか。", "en": "Do you know where they decided to hold the meeting?", "fr": "Savez-vous où la réunion a finalement été fixée ?", "grammar": "〜か（間接疑問）", "focus": "決まる"},
    {"jp": "彼がなぜ怒っているか、ぜんぜん分からない。", "en": "I have no idea at all why he is angry.", "fr": "Je ne comprends pas du tout pourquoi il est en colère.", "grammar": "〜か（間接疑問）", "focus": "怒る"},
    {"jp": "心配なことがあれば、いつでも遠慮しないで相談してね。", "en": "If anything worries you, come and talk to me any time, don't hold back.", "fr": "Si quelque chose t'inquiète, viens m'en parler quand tu veux, sans hésiter.", "grammar": "何でも／誰でも／いつでも／どこでも", "focus": "遠慮"},
    {"jp": "この市の図書館は、市民なら誰でも利用できます。", "en": "Anyone who lives in this city can use its library.", "fr": "Tous les habitants de la ville peuvent utiliser sa bibliothèque.", "grammar": "何でも／誰でも／いつでも／どこでも", "focus": "市民"},
    {"jp": "次の駅で、特急に乗り換えたほうがいいでしょうか。", "en": "Would it be better to change to the limited express at the next station?", "fr": "Est-ce que je ferais mieux de prendre l'express à la prochaine gare ?", "grammar": "〜でしょうか", "focus": "乗り換える"},
    {"jp": "来週の火曜日、先生のご都合はよろしいでしょうか。", "en": "Would next Tuesday be convenient for you, professor?", "fr": "Mardi prochain, est-ce que cela vous conviendrait, professeur ?", "grammar": "〜でしょうか", "focus": "都合"},
    {"jp": "事故で電車が止まって、空港まで三時間もかかった。", "en": "The train stopped because of an accident, and it took me a full three hours to get to the airport.", "fr": "Le train s'est arrêté à cause d'un accident, et il m'a fallu trois bonnes heures pour arriver à l'aéroport.", "grammar": "〜も（強調）", "focus": "空港"},
    {"jp": "近所の金持ちは、車を五台も持っているらしい。", "en": "Apparently the rich man in the neighbourhood owns as many as five cars.", "fr": "Il paraît que le riche du quartier possède pas moins de cinq voitures.", "grammar": "〜も（強調）", "focus": "金持ち"},
    {"jp": "けさは寝坊しました。それで、急行に間に合いませんでした。", "en": "I overslept this morning. That's why I missed the express.", "fr": "Je ne me suis pas réveillé à temps ce matin. C'est pour ça que j'ai raté l'express.", "grammar": "それで", "focus": "寝坊"},
    {"jp": "駅でさいふを拾った。それで、警察に届けた。", "en": "I found a wallet at the station, so I took it to the police.", "fr": "J'ai trouvé un portefeuille à la gare, alors je l'ai apporté à la police.", "grammar": "それで", "focus": "警察"},
    {"jp": "この下宿は駅から遠くて不便だ。それに、冷房もない。", "en": "This lodging is far from the station and inconvenient. What's more, it has no air conditioning.", "fr": "Ce logement est loin de la gare et peu pratique. En plus, il n'y a pas de climatisation.", "grammar": "それに", "focus": "下宿"},
    {"jp": "あの旅館は景色がすばらしい。それに、食事もおいしい。", "en": "That inn has wonderful views. Besides, the food is delicious.", "fr": "Cette auberge a une vue magnifique. En plus, les repas sont délicieux.", "grammar": "それに", "focus": "旅館"},
    {"jp": "ところで、美術館の展覧会にはもう行きましたか。", "en": "By the way, have you been to the exhibition at the art museum yet?", "fr": "Au fait, vous êtes déjà allé voir l'exposition au musée d'art ?", "grammar": "ところで", "focus": "展覧会"},
    {"jp": "ところで、お嬢さんは今年、大学を卒業するんですか。", "en": "By the way, is your daughter graduating from university this year?", "fr": "Au fait, votre fille termine ses études à l'université cette année ?", "grammar": "ところで", "focus": "卒業"},
